# TODO - Clang C frontend integration

## Objective

Use Clang as the C parser, type system, constant evaluator, source-location
provider, and AST frontend instead of building another C parser.

## Acceptance

- Pinned Clang parsing/type information is normalized deterministically and
  host-only frontend details do not leak into the portable compiler IR or target
  semantics.
- The stage has deterministic input/output form, rejects malformed or
  unsupported input explicitly, and preserves source/profile provenance needed
  downstream.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `compiler/`, `src/`, `tests/compiler/`.
- Required evidence: golden normalized-stage fixtures, deterministic hashes,
  physical-path relocation equality, exact source/profile provenance,
  and
  accepted/rejected semantic normalization cases. Portable IR/lowering evidence
  remains downstream because `typed-compiler-ir` depends on this task.
- Implemented product evidence: governed `src/compiler/c-frontend/` owns a
  host-neutral frontend port, exact Clang 22.1.8 LibTooling adapter, closed
  `malbolge-c-frontend-v1` artifact contract, and `/W4 /WX` native composition.
- Implemented determinism evidence: the checked-in semantic golden records exact
  source SHA-256, logical source identity, source-byte spans, normalized types,
  operations, constant evaluation, references, and declaration semantics.
- Implemented relocation evidence: identical source bytes under distinct
  physical paths produce byte-identical normalized artifacts for one logical
  source ID;
  private LLVM/repository paths do not enter output.
- Implemented ABI evidence: ordinary enum representation follows
  `malbolge-c32-v1` (`i32` when representable, otherwise `u32`) rather than
  Clang's wasm default choice; fixed C23 underlying types are retained and a
  value domain outside both ABI choices fails closed.
- Implemented declaration evidence: storage class/duration, linkage,
  declaration/tentative-definition/definition state, explicit `inline`, and
  parameter `register` state are preserved for downstream typed IR.
- Implemented failure evidence: unsupported `_BitInt`, impossible default enum
  domain, malformed C, and escaping logical source identity fail before partial
  artifact publication with `MALBOLGE-FRONTEND-001` through `004` families.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `deterministic-c-to-malbolge-abi`.

- Completion evidence on 2026-08-08: the governed `src/compiler/c-frontend/`
  function builds against exact LLVM/Clang 22.1.8 with C++20, `/W4 /WX`, and
